# Godot 4
.godot/
*.translation

# .uid files are NOT ignored. Godot 4.4+ writes one per script and resource, and
# they are what keeps references stable when a file is renamed or moved. Ignoring
# them makes every clone regenerate different IDs and breaks scene references.

# Generated content — reproducible from tools/, never committed
assets/generated/
# Fetched fonts — reproduced by tools/assets/fetch_liberation_sans.sh from a
# pinned SHA-256, same rule as doctest. ATTRIBUTION.md records the license.
/assets/fonts/

# GDExtension build artifacts
.sconsign.dblite
.sconf_temp/
config.log
*.os
*.obj
*.o
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.lib
*.pdb
*.exp
*.a
/bin/

# Godot export output
/build/
/export/

# Blender
*.blend1
*.blend2

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Look-dev stills — render output, reproducible from tools/shots/shoot.sh
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. Written as a bare `shots/` this matched ANY
# directory named shots at any depth, which silently excluded tools/shots/ --
# so the M1 still-capture harness itself was never committed, even though
# ROADMAP.md M1 lists it as delivered. It kept working locally, which is why
# nothing noticed. See issue #106.
/shots/

# Reference material — copyrighted photographs and FIA documents, looked at
# and never shipped. REFERENCES.md records what each file is and where it
# came from; the files themselves must not enter history.
/refs/

# LightmapGI bake products are NOT ignored, despite being generated output.
#
# The §16 rule says generated content stays out of version control, and the
# first attempt here followed it. That is wrong for a bake: the scene file
# stores a hard ext_resource reference to its .lmbake, so ignoring the bake
# leaves every fresh clone with a scene that cannot load. Reproducing one is
# also not something a build can do -- it needs the GUI editor and GPU time
# (ADR-0022).
#
# They are on LFS. Revisit the size question at M5, where a full track bake is
# a different order of magnitude than this test scene's 412 KB.

# doctest, fetched by tools/assets/fetch_doctest.sh with a pinned checksum.
#
# Ignored for the same reason assets/generated/ is: it is reproducible from a
# tool in this repo, and the tool pins the version and the SHA-256, so a clone
# gets the same 7,000-line header rather than one somebody edited. Anchored,
# because a bare `doctest/` is exactly the pattern that cost this project its
# whole shots harness -- issue #106.
/third_party/doctest/

# The unit-test binary. Built by tests/run.sh into bin/, which is already
# ignored above, but named here so it is obvious it is not meant to be shipped.
/bin/tests/

# Godot import sidecars for files under docs/ that are documentation rather than
# resources.
#
# `docs/circuits/*.csv` are the design's walked centerline and speed profile. They
# are read by `tools/circuits/render_circuit.py` with Python and by a human with
# their eyes; nothing loads them through `res://`. Godot's CSV importer picks them
# up anyway on the first editor import and drops a `.import` beside each, which is
# then untracked noise in `git status` forever.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash, which is the whole lesson of issue #106: a bare
# pattern matched `tools/shots/` once and kept an entire harness out of the repo.
/docs/**/*.import
